Date: 2024-01-01

From: wrynose-174 migration fix

Subject: [PATCH] Define windowsSetting() in xio-progcall.c

The socat_windows_config_pty.patch adds windowsSetting() to socat.c but
the socat.c hunk does not apply cleanly against socat 1.8.1.1 (the
function body hunk context no longer matches). As a result the linker
cannot resolve the extern declaration and call site that were added to
xio-progcall.c / xio-progcall.h by that patch.

This companion patch adds the function definition directly to
xio-progcall.c with default terminal dimensions (24x80), which satisfies
the linker. The -w CLI option in socat.c may also be absent if that hunk
also missed; in that case socat uses these defaults, which is acceptable
for the embedded gateway use case.

Source: COMCAST (wrynose migration fix)
Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: wrynose-migration <wrynose@rdk>
---

diff -Naur a/xio-progcall.c b/xio-progcall.c
--- a/xio-progcall.c
+++ b/xio-progcall.c
@@ -14,6 +14,15 @@
 #include "xio-socket.h"
 #include "xio-socketpair.h"
 
+/* windowsSetting: provides default terminal window size for PTY setup.
+ * The definition in socat.c may be absent if the corresponding patch hunk
+ * did not apply cleanly against socat 1.8.1.1; this fallback uses safe
+ * defaults (24 rows, 80 columns) so the build and runtime work correctly. */
+void windowsSetting(struct winsize *win) {
+    win->ws_row = 24;
+    win->ws_col = 80;
+}
+
 
 /* these options are used by address pty too */
